note ref/mem.om: omc reference of mkir fixture mem (prints ok, exit = (s + write's count) low byte).
note Omega passes no global as an argument (error 19) and writes no chk.bounds with e = 2, so the fixture's
note fill(REF src) is inline here and its chk.bounds src 298 2 (which passes) has no counterpart.
global src uchar 300
text msg "ok\n"
fn main to int
for i ulong 300
put src i uchar and mul i 7 255
end
b = new ulong 600 0
for i ulong 300
put b add i 300 add ulong get src i i
end
s = ulong 0
for i ulong 600
s = add s mul get b i add i 1
end
w = write 1 msg 0 3
ret int and add s ulong w 255
end
